<p>It serves as the foundation of human civilization, allowing societies to transition from nomadic hunting to settled communities. Farmers work hard in fields and pastures using both traditional methods and modern tools like tractors to grow vital crops such as rice, wheat, fruits, and vegetables, alongside raising livestock for milk, eggs, and meat. Beyond feeding the global population, agriculture drives economic growth, creates millions of rural and industrial jobs, and supplies essential raw materials for manufacturing, textiles, and trade. Today, sustainable and organic farming practices are increasingly vital to protect soil health, conserve water, and secure food resources for the future</p>
